# Spec Kit and agent state.
# The shared parts -- .specify/ templates, scripts, memory/constitution.md, and the
# .claude/skills/ commands -- ARE committed; they are how work happens here.
# These are per-machine or credential-bearing and are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.credentials.json

# Agent worktrees live inside the repository, so without this they show up as
# untracked source and get scanned by anything that walks the tree.
.claude/worktrees/

# A tool-agnostic copy of CLAUDE.md and of .claude/skills/, generated by the Spec Kit
# CLI. Committing it would give the project two sources of truth for its own rules,
# which is the thing the constitution exists to prevent. Regenerate it locally if a
# tool needs it; do not let it drift into the repository.
AGENTS.md
.agents/
